The mass, in kilograms, of fruit picked from a tree each day is modelled by $X$ with probability density function $f(x)=\frac{x-2}{2}$ on $[2,4]$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-0.4, xmax=5.2, ymin=-0.14, ymax=1.3, samples=100, clip=false, width=8cm, height=6cm, xtick={0,1,2,3,4}, ytick={0.25,0.5,0.75,1}]
\addplot[thick, domain=2:4] {(x-2)/2};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the mean mass picked per day.

questions.solution_text:
$E(X)=\int_{2}^{4}x\cdot\frac{x-2}{2}\,dx$
$=\frac{1}{2}\int_{2}^{4}(x^{2}-2x)\,dx$
$=\frac{1}{2}\left[\frac{x^{3}}{3}-x^{2}\right]_{2}^{4}$
$=\frac{1}{2}\left(\frac{16}{3}+\frac{4}{3}\right)$
$=\frac{1}{2}\times\frac{20}{3}$
$=\frac{10}{3}$
The mean mass is $\frac{10}{3}$ kg.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-0.4, xmax=5.2, ymin=-0.14, ymax=1.3, samples=100, clip=false, width=8cm, height=6cm, xtick={0,1,2,3,4}, ytick={0.25,0.5,0.75,1}]
\addplot[thick, domain=2:4] {(x-2)/2};
\draw[dashed] (axis cs:3.3333,0) -- (axis cs:3.3333,0.6667);
\node[above left] at (axis cs:3.3333,0.7) {$\mu=\frac{10}{3}$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

questions.question_text:
The continuous random variable $X$ has probability density function $f(x)=\frac{3x^{2}}{343}$ on $[0,7]$, mean $\frac{21}{4}$ and variance $\frac{147}{80}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-0.9, xmax=8.4, ymin=-0.08, ymax=0.6, samples=100, clip=false, width=8cm, height=6cm, xtick={0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7}, ytick={0.2,0.4}]
\addplot[thick, domain=0:7] {3*x*x/343};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the probability that $X$ lies within one standard deviation of the mean, correct to two decimal places.

questions.solution_text:
$\sigma=\sqrt{\frac{147}{80}}$
$\approx 1.3556$
$\mu-\sigma\approx 3.8944$
$\mu+\sigma\approx 6.6056$
$P(3.8944\le X\le 6.6056)=\left[\frac{x^{3}}{343}\right]_{3.8944}^{6.6056}$
$=\frac{288.22-59.07}{343}$
$=\frac{229.15}{343}$
$\approx 0.67$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-0.9, xmax=8.4, ymin=-0.08, ymax=0.6, samples=100, clip=false, width=8cm, height=6cm, xtick={0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7}, ytick={0.2,0.4}]
\addplot[draw=none, fill=gray!35, domain=3.8944:6.6056] {3*x*x/343} \closedcycle;
\addplot[thick, domain=0:7] {3*x*x/343};
\draw[dashed] (axis cs:5.25,0) -- (axis cs:5.25,0.2411);
\node[above left] at (axis cs:5.25,0.47) {$\mu=\frac{21}{4}$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
